--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/core/src/multipart/upload_part.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,1601 @@
+//! `UploadPart`'s **staging**: one part's bytes into an `Open` session, through the slot reserve,
+//! an owned intent per chunk, the lease renewal, and the part commit or the live-session
+//! compensation that ends every attempt (#657, slice 4 of #636).
+//!
+//! [`upload_part`] stages a part and answers in the landed vocabulary ([`UploadPartOutcome`],
+//! [`Refusal`]); [`reserve_slot`] is its first step alone, answering [`ReserveOutcome`]. Every
+//! batch is a row of proposal 0016's batch inventory (`0016:658-660`, `:673`), under decision 5
+//! (`0016:1507-1793`):
+//!
+//! | Batch | Preconditions | Mutations |
+//! |---|---|---|
+//! | reserve | `require(mpu:<id> == Open@E)`, `require_absent(slot:<id>:<k>)` | put the slot |
+//! | intent, one per chunk | `require(mpu:<id> == Open@E)`, `require(slot == prior)`, `require_absent(desired:dserver:<S>)` for every server `S` in the chunk's placement, `require_absent(sidx:<id>:<n>:<chunk>)` | put the owned `sidx:` entry carrying that placement; rewrite the slot |
+//! | renewal | `require(mpu:<id> == Open@E)`, `require(slot == prior)` | put every owned `sidx:` entry with the new lease; rewrite the slot |
+//! | commit | `require(mpu:<id> == Open@E)`, `require_absent(part:<id>:<n>)` or `require(part == prior)`, `require(slot == prior)`, and on a re-upload `require_absent(retire:bytes:<token>)` | put `part:` and `psum:`; delete the slot and every owned `sidx:` entry; on a re-upload, put the replaced part's chunks as a `retire:bytes:` obligation |
+//! | compensation | `require(mpu:<id> == Open@E)`, `require(slot == prior)`, and with chunks staged `require_absent(retire:bytes:<token>)` | put this attempt's chunks as a `retire:bytes:` obligation; delete the slot and every owned `sidx:` entry |
+//!
+//! An obligation's token is `s:<upload-id>:<E>:<part-number>:<attempt-id>` (`0016:358-366`), so
+//! its key is minted once per attempt and epoch.
+//!
+//! Production calls nothing here yet: the S3 verb that will is #669, under 0016's rule that the
+//! reaper ships in the same release (`0016:236-268`). The in-process races are pinned by
+//! `crates/core/tests/multipart_upload_part.rs`; their seeded Tier-0 DST coverage is
+//! deferred: #660.
+//!
+//! # What holds (**C-1**, `docs/principles.md` §5)
+//!
+//! * **A staged fragment is named before it exists.** A chunk's fragments are written only after
+//!   the intent that puts its owned `sidx:` entry, with the planned placement, has committed.
+//!   While the session is `Open`, an owned entry leaves only in a batch that puts a `part:` record
+//!   or a `retire:bytes:` obligation naming the same chunk; after a fence it is the drain's.
+//! * **No owned record after the fence, and none on a draining server.** Every intent and renewal
+//!   is fenced on the session being `Open@E`, and every intent on no planned server having a drain
+//!   record. Placement selects from the topology minus every server with a drain record, read from
+//!   the store before each chunk, and a drain recorded between that read and the intent makes the
+//!   chunk plan again without that server. A drain never refuses the part.
+//! * **An `Open` session is never answered `NoSuchUpload`.** `NoSuchUpload` answers only a session
+//!   that is absent or has left `Open`, whose residue is then the drain's (`0016:1600-1606`). Every
+//!   other ending of an attempt releases its slot through the compensation, unless a commit of it
+//!   may still land or the compensation itself cannot land (a store fault, its rounds spent); the
+//!   error then reports [`Residue::Left`], and the slot is residue counted against the cap until
+//!   the session's teardown, as a crashed attempt's is.
+//!
+//! # One slot, one writer, at most one landing
+//!
+//! Every batch after the reserve requires the attempt's own slot at exactly the bytes it last saw
+//! land, and every such batch either rewrites the slot with a strictly later lease or deletes it.
+//! So of the batches that require one slot value, **at most one can ever land**. That is what makes
+//! an unknown outcome safe to carry (`0016:1630-1651`): the attempt keeps the batch as "may still
+//! land" and sends its next batch against the same slot bytes, and the first read that finds the
+//! slot moved says which one landed. A batch is recognised by what only it writes: an intent by
+//! its owned entry's exact bytes, a renewal by its slot bytes, the commit by its `part:` bytes
+//! (its chunk ids are its own, so no other attempt writes them), a compensation by its obligation.
+//!
+//! # Runtime-free (ADR-0009), and one clock
+//!
+//! Core reads no clock of its own, draws no randomness and never sleeps here. The caller hands in
+//! its clock (`now`), the chunk ids (`next_id`) and the write window `W_write`. The readings of
+//! `now` stamp the attempt's leases, which the reaper judges (`0016:349`), and each staged write's
+//! deadline, which the D server judges (`0016:1480`, `:1567-1578`); both lifecycles run on the one
+//! deployment wall clock, so `now` must read that clock, the one the session's `clock_source`
+//! names.
+
+use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};
+use std::fmt;
+use std::num::NonZeroU64;
+
+use bytes::Bytes;
+use futures_util::{Stream, StreamExt};
+use wyrd_traits::{
+    BoxError, ChunkId, CommitOutcome, CommitUnknownResult, DServerId, FragmentId, MetadataStore,
+    PlacementChunkStore, WriteBatch,
+};
+
+use super::{
+    decode_part_record, decode_part_summary, decode_session_record, mpu_key, parse_psum_key,
+    parse_slot_key, part_key, psum_key, psum_range, sidx_key, slot_key, slot_range,
+    upload_part_answer, AttemptId, Backpressure, Digest, DigestBuilder, OwnedEntry, PartNumber,
+    PartRecord, RecordError, Refusal, ReserveOutcome, RetireObligation, SessionState, SlotIndex,
+    SlotRecord, StagedPlacement, UploadId, UploadPartAnswer, UploadPartOutcome,
+    MAX_COMPLETE_ATTEMPTS, MAX_INFLIGHT_PARTS, MAX_PART_CHUNKS, MAX_STAGED_CHUNKS,
+};
+use crate::metadata::{self, ChunkRef, EcScheme, DESIRED_DSERVER_PREFIX};
+use crate::placement::{select_distinct_domains, SelectorError, Topology};
+use crate::write::encode_chunk;
+
+/// How many times one batch of an attempt is sent at most: [`MAX_COMPLETE_ATTEMPTS`] `+ 1`, the
+/// size of [`super::abort::ABORT_ROUNDS`] and for its reason.
+///
+/// Each batch gets its own budget: each chunk's intent, each renewal, the commit and the
+/// compensation (the reserve has its own, [`MAX_INFLIGHT_PARTS`] `+` this). A round is spent by a
+/// send that did not land: a conflict no re-read explains (on TiKV, a lock another writer held,
+/// with nothing moved), an outcome the store could not report, a drain recorded on a planned
+/// server (the chunk plans again), or the session moving to a later `Open` epoch (the
+/// compensation follows it, and a session makes at most [`MAX_COMPLETE_ATTEMPTS`] such moves). It
+/// bounds the work, not correctness: an attempt that spends a budget ends with an error that says
+/// whether a batch of it may still land.
+pub const UPLOAD_PART_ROUNDS: u32 = MAX_COMPLETE_ATTEMPTS + 1;
+
+/// What one `UploadPart` stages. Every field is the caller's: core mints no identity and reads
+/// no clock.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]
+pub struct UploadPartRequest<'a> {
+    /// The session the part is for.
+    pub upload_id: &'a UploadId,
+    /// The part number.
+    pub part_number: PartNumber,
+    /// This attempt's identity: a fresh 128-bit token from the caller's randomness, never reused.
+    /// It is stamped into the attempt's slot and into the token of any obligation it installs.
+    pub attempt_id: &'a AttemptId,
+    /// How each chunk is erasure-coded.
+    pub scheme: EcScheme,
+    /// Bytes per chunk; the last chunk may be shorter. `0` is read as `1`, as the streaming write
+    /// reads it.
+    pub chunk_size: usize,
+    /// The D servers and failure domains placement selects from. Every server with a drain
+    /// record is removed from it before each selection ([`Topology::excluding`]).
+    pub topology: &'a Topology,
+    /// How long a lease the attempt stamps lasts, its slot's and its owned entries'. They are
+    /// renewed half a TTL ahead, as the streaming write renews its leases.
+    pub lease_ttl_millis: NonZeroU64,
+    /// `W_write`, the window a staged fragment write must land in (`0016:1480`): every fragment
+    /// of a chunk carries the deadline `t_auth + W_write`, where `t_auth` is the clock reading
+    /// taken before that chunk's intent was sent. The deployed value is the custodian's
+    /// `W_WRITE_MILLIS`, which core cannot import (ADR-0010), so the caller passes it; there is no
+    /// default, and no write goes out without a deadline.
+    pub write_window_millis: NonZeroU64,
+}
+
+/// An `UploadPart` that ended with neither an answer nor a refusal.
+///
+/// # Error class
+///
+/// [`wyrd_traits::classify`] reads [`Self::InDoubt`] as
+/// [`ErrorClass::Indeterminate`](wyrd_traits::ErrorClass::Indeterminate), whatever stopped the
+/// attempt: its [`source`](std::error::Error::source) is the store's own
+/// [`CommitUnknownResult`]. [`Self::Stopped`] keeps its cause's class.
+#[derive(Debug)]
+pub enum UploadPartError {
+    /// A batch of this attempt may have landed, or may still land, and the attempt stopped before
+    /// a read could say which. Never "nothing was written".
+    InDoubt(Box<InDoubt>),
+    /// The attempt stopped, and no batch of it is in doubt.
+    Stopped(Box<Stopped>),
+}
+
+/// What an [`UploadPartError::InDoubt`] reports.
+#[derive(Debug)]
+pub struct InDoubt {
+    /// The session.
+    pub upload_id: UploadId,
+    /// The part number.
+    pub part_number: PartNumber,
+    /// The attempt whose batch is in doubt.
+    pub attempt_id: AttemptId,
+    /// Whether a batch of this attempt may still be applied **after** it returned
+    /// ([`CommitUnknownResult::may_still_commit`]).
+    pub may_still_commit: bool,
+    /// The store's report of the unknown outcome that keeps the doubt: the first that said
+    /// `may_still_commit`, or else the latest one no read has settled. It is the error's
+    /// [`source`](std::error::Error::source).
+    pub outcome: CommitUnknownResult,
+    /// What stopped the attempt before it could settle the doubt.
+    pub cause: Stop,
+}
+
+/// What an [`UploadPartError::Stopped`] reports.
+#[derive(Debug)]
+pub struct Stopped {
+    /// The session.
+    pub upload_id: UploadId,
+    /// The part number.
+    pub part_number: PartNumber,
+    /// The attempt that stopped.
+    pub attempt_id: AttemptId,
+    /// What stopped it.
+    pub cause: Stop,
+    /// What it left behind.
+    pub residue: Residue,
+}
+
+/// What a stopped attempt left in the store.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub enum Residue {
+    /// Nothing of it is live: it holds no slot and no owned entry. It reserved none, or its
+    /// compensation landed and a `retire:bytes:` obligation owes the chunks it staged.
+    Released,
+    /// Its slot and every owned `sidx:` entry it staged are left in place: counted against the
+    /// session's in-flight cap and reclaimed with the session at its teardown, as a crashed
+    /// attempt's are (`0016:1744-1764`, F11a).
+    Left,
+}
+
+/// What stopped an `UploadPart` ([`InDoubt::cause`], [`Stopped::cause`]).
+#[derive(Debug)]
+pub enum Stop {
+    /// One batch was sent [`UPLOAD_PART_ROUNDS`] times without landing (for the reserve, its own
+    /// budget), and nothing a read found settled it.
+    RoundsSpent {
+        /// Sends made.
+        rounds: u32,
+    },
+    /// The topology minus the servers with a drain record has too few failure domains for the
+    /// scheme: no placement exists that lands nothing on a draining server.
+    Placement(SelectorError),
+    /// A chunk could not be erasure-coded.
+    Encode(BoxError),
+    /// A staged fragment write failed, or was refused past its deadline.
+    Fragments(BoxError),
+    /// The part's body stream failed.
+    Body(BoxError),
+    /// A lease or a write deadline would pass `u64::MAX` milliseconds.
+    ClockOverflow,
+    /// This attempt's slot moved while its session stayed `Open@E`, and no batch of this attempt
+    /// explains it. Only this attempt writes that key while the session is `Open`.
+    SlotLost,
+    /// The owned-entry key of a fresh chunk id already holds a value no batch of this attempt
+    /// wrote: the caller's chunk ids collided.
+    ChunkIdTaken {
+        /// The chunk id.
+        chunk: ChunkId,
+    },
+    /// The key of an obligation this attempt installs already holds a value no batch of it wrote.
+    /// A token is minted once per attempt and epoch (`0016:358-373`), so this is damage a retry
+    /// cannot settle.
+    ObligationKeyTaken {
+        /// The `retire:` key, as UTF-8 (lossy).
+        key: String,
+    },
+    /// A stored record would not decode, or a value this attempt built would not (ADR-0045).
+    Record(RecordError),
+    /// A store operation failed.
+    Store(BoxError),
+}
+
+impl fmt::Display for UploadPartError {
+    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
+        match self {
+            Self::InDoubt(doubt) => write!(
+                f,
+                "multipart upload part: upload {} part {} attempt {} is in doubt: a batch of this \
+                 attempt {}; re-read the part and the slot to learn which landed ({})",
+                doubt.upload_id,
+                doubt.part_number,
+                doubt.attempt_id,
+                if doubt.may_still_commit {
+                    "may still be applied"
+                } else {
+                    "may have been applied"
+                },
+                doubt.cause,
+            ),
+            Self::Stopped(stopped) => write!(
+                f,
+                "multipart upload part: upload {} part {} attempt {}: {}; no batch of this \
+                 attempt is in doubt, and {}",
+                stopped.upload_id,
+                stopped.part_number,
+                stopped.attempt_id,
+                stopped.cause,
+                match stopped.residue {
+                    Residue::Released => "it holds no slot and no staged entry",
+                    Residue::Left => {
+                        "its slot and staged entries are left for the session's teardown"
+                    }
+                },
+            ),
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+impl fmt::Display for Stop {
+    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
+        match self {
+            Self::RoundsSpent { rounds } => {
+                write!(f, "one batch was sent {rounds} times and did not land")
+            }
+            Self::Placement(refused) => {
+                write!(f, "no placement avoids every draining D server: {refused}")
+            }
+            Self::Encode(fault) => write!(f, "a chunk could not be erasure-coded: {fault}"),
+            Self::Fragments(fault) => write!(f, "a staged fragment write failed: {fault}"),
+            Self::Body(fault) => write!(f, "the part body failed: {fault}"),
+            Self::ClockOverflow => {
+                f.write_str("a lease or a write deadline would pass u64::MAX milliseconds")
+            }
+            Self::SlotLost => f.write_str(
+                "the attempt's slot moved while the session stayed Open, and no batch of the \
+                 attempt explains it",
+            ),
+            Self::ChunkIdTaken { chunk } => write!(
+                f,
+                "the owned entry of fresh chunk {chunk} is already taken by bytes this attempt \
+                 did not write"
+            ),
+            Self::ObligationKeyTaken { key } => write!(
+                f,
+                "the obligation key {key} is already taken by bytes this attempt did not write; \
+                 this is damage a retry cannot settle"
+            ),
+            Self::Record(torn) => write!(f, "a record is invalid: {torn}"),
+            Self::Store(fault) => write!(f, "store fault: {fault}"),
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+impl std::error::Error for UploadPartError {
+    fn source(&self) -> Option<&(dyn std::error::Error + 'static)> {
+        match self {
+            // The unknown outcome, never the stop cause: `classify` stops at the first seam type
+            // on the chain, and an attempt in doubt must read `Indeterminate`.
+            Self::InDoubt(doubt) => Some(&doubt.outcome),
+            Self::Stopped(stopped) => match &stopped.cause {
+                Stop::Placement(refused) => Some(refused),
+                Stop::Encode(fault)
+                | Stop::Fragments(fault)
+                | Stop::Body(fault)
+                | Stop::Store(fault) => Some(fault.as_ref()),
+                Stop::Record(torn) => Some(torn),
+                Stop::RoundsSpent { .. }
+                | Stop::ClockOverflow
+                | Stop::SlotLost
+                | Stop::ChunkIdTaken { .. }
+                | Stop::ObligationKeyTaken { .. } => None,
+            },
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/// **The slot reserve** (`0016:349`, `:658`, `:1676-1719`) on its own: claim one in-flight slot
+/// `slot:<id>:<k>` of the session for `attempt_id`, stamped `now_millis` with a lease of
+/// `lease_ttl_millis`. [`upload_part`] runs exactly this as its first step.
+///
+/// Read the session and the bounded `slot:<id>:` range; refuse unless the session is `Open`
+/// ([`upload_part_answer`]: [`Refusal::NoSuchUpload`], with nothing written); take the lowest free
+/// index in `[0, MAX_INFLIGHT_PARTS)` and commit `require(mpu == Open@E)` +
+/// `require_absent(slot:<id>:<k>)` + the slot. A full range is
+/// [`Refusal::SlowDown`] with [`Backpressure::InflightParts`]: the key space is the cap, so a
+/// reserver that loses an index takes the next free one from a fresh read.
+///
+/// The slot record is built once, so every send puts the same bytes, and its attempt id makes
+/// those bytes this attempt's alone. A read that finds them anywhere in the range is this
+/// attempt's slot, adopted: that is how a reserve whose outcome was unknown but which landed is
+/// settled (`0016:1699-1706`). After an outcome that **may still land**, an absent index proves
+/// nothing, so the next send goes to the **same** index with the same bytes; the two are
+/// exclusive through `require_absent`, so at most one lands (`0016:1707-1716`). It moves on only
+/// once that index holds another attempt's slot, or the session has moved.
+///
+/// It makes at most [`MAX_INFLIGHT_PARTS`] `+` [`UPLOAD_PART_ROUNDS`] commits. When they are spent
+/// it ends with an error, [`UploadPartError::InDoubt`] while a reserve of it may still land: no
+/// [`Backpressure`] arm says "a slot of yours may yet appear", and a slot that does appear is
+/// residue counted against the cap until the session's teardown (F11a), as `0016:1716-1718`
+/// accepts.
+pub async fn reserve_slot(
+    store: &impl MetadataStore,
+    upload_id: &UploadId,
+    part_number: PartNumber,
+    attempt_id: &AttemptId,
+    now_millis: u64,
+    lease_ttl_millis: NonZeroU64,
+) -> Result<ReserveOutcome, UploadPartError> {
+    let ids = Ids {
+        upload_id,
+        part_number,
+        attempt_id,
+    };
+    Ok(
+        match reserve(store, &ids, now_millis, lease_ttl_millis).await? {
+            Reserve::Held(held) => ReserveOutcome::Reserved {
+                index: held.index,
+                attempt_id: attempt_id.clone(),
+            },
+            Reserve::Refused(refusal) => ReserveOutcome::Refused(refusal),
+        },
+    )
+}
+
+/// **`UploadPart`**: stage `body` as part `request.part_number` of the session and commit it
+/// (`0016:658-660`, `:673`, decision 5), answering in the landed vocabulary. No production path
+/// calls this yet (#669 will).
+///
+/// # The steps
+///
+/// 1. **Reserve** a slot ([`reserve_slot`]). A refusal there is the answer.
+/// 2. **Stage** each `chunk_size` piece of `body`, in order:
+///    * if the clock has passed half the lease, **renew** first: one batch puts every owned entry
+///      with the new lease and rewrites the slot with it, under `require(mpu == Open@E)` and
+///      `require(slot == prior)` (`0016:349`, `:659`);
+///    * **plan** the chunk's placement against `request.topology` minus every server that has a
+///      drain record ([`crate::metadata::DESIRED_DSERVER_PREFIX`]);
+///    * read the clock once as `t_auth`, and commit the **intent** (module table). If it conflicts
+///      and a planned server now has a drain record, plan again without it;
+///    * only then write the chunk's fragments, each to its planned server with the deadline
+///      `t_auth + W_write`, the same for every fragment however late it is dispatched.
+///
+///    A part that would stage more than [`MAX_PART_CHUNKS`] chunks is refused
+///    [`Refusal::EntityTooLarge`] before the chunk past the cap is staged.
+/// 3. **Quiesce**: a last renewal if the clock has moved, so the lease covers the commit
+///    (`0016:1720-1733`). No renewal runs beside the commit: the steps are sequential.
+/// 4. **Commit** the part: read the part key and the bounded `psum:<id>:` range. If the session's
+///    other parts plus this one would hold more than [`MAX_STAGED_CHUNKS`] chunks, refuse
+///    [`Refusal::EntityTooLarge`]. That read is deliberately not fenced: the overshoot concurrent
+///    commits can add is bounded by the slot cap and charged in `U_ref` (`0016:1443-1450`). Then
+///    one batch (module table). The part record is built once, so every send of it puts the same
+///    bytes; its digest is the SHA-256 of the body (ADR-0047).
+///
+/// Every refusal after the reserve, and every stop but one, **compensates** first: one batch puts
+/// this attempt's staged chunks as a `retire:bytes:` obligation, releases the slot and deletes the
+/// owned entries (`0016:673`, `:1420-1432`), so an `Open` session never fills its slots with a
+/// refused part's residue. The one exception is a stop while a commit of this attempt may still
+/// land: a compensation then would race the part it may have committed, so the attempt returns
+/// the doubt instead.
+///
+/// # A batch that did not land (`0016:1597-1651`)
+///
+/// Read the session, the slot, the part and the keys only this attempt's batches write, and
+/// judge from what the store holds, never by inference:
+///
+/// * a batch of this attempt found landed is answered for what it did: a commit found landed is
+///   [`UploadPartOutcome::Committed`], and the slot is never released twice;
+/// * the session absent or no longer `Open`: [`Refusal::NoSuchUpload`], with no compensation —
+///   the residue is the drain's;
+/// * the session `Open` at a later epoch (a Complete fenced it and rolled back): compensate
+///   under that epoch and answer [`Refusal::OperationAborted`];
+/// * the part key moved (a rival attempt committed this part number first): compensate and
+///   answer [`Refusal::OperationAborted`];
+/// * a drain record on a planned server (intent): plan again;
+/// * nothing moved: send the same batch again. That is the case for a conflict no read explains,
+///   and for a batch whose outcome was unknown, found not landed. With `may_still_commit == false`
+///   that read settles it; with `true` it proves nothing, so the attempt neither answers nor
+///   compensates on it, and its next send requires the same slot bytes as the batch in doubt.
+///
+/// A [`CommitUnknownResult`] is never read as a conflict. A commit whose outcome was unknown is
+/// answered `Committed` only when the part key holds **exactly** the bytes this attempt built: a
+/// part found there but not those bytes (the prior part of a re-upload, a rival's) proves only
+/// that this commit has not landed yet.
+///
+/// # Termination
+///
+/// At most [`UPLOAD_PART_ROUNDS`] sends per batch: one intent and at most one renewal per chunk,
+/// at most [`MAX_PART_CHUNKS`] chunks, then one renewal, one commit and at most one compensation,
+/// with a bounded number of reads between two sends. Each store and chunk-store call is bounded by that store's
+/// own contract (every operation terminates; a fragment write past its deadline is refused by the
+/// D server, #638), and `body` by its caller.
+///
+/// **Not cancel-safe once a batch is sent.** Dropping the future after that can leave a batch that
+/// lands with no answer naming it; its residue is then counted against the session's slots until
+/// the teardown, like a crashed attempt's. Bound an attempt through the stores' own deadlines,
+/// never by dropping the future.
+pub async fn upload_part<B>(
+    store: &impl MetadataStore,
+    chunks: &impl PlacementChunkStore,
+    request: &UploadPartRequest<'_>,
+    body: B,
+    mut now: impl FnMut() -> u64,
+    mut next_id: impl FnMut() -> ChunkId,
+) -> Result<UploadPartOutcome, UploadPartError>
+where
+    B: Stream<Item = wyrd_traits::Result<Bytes>> + Unpin,
+{
+    let ids = Ids {
+        upload_id: request.upload_id,
+        part_number: request.part_number,
+        attempt_id: request.attempt_id,
+    };
+    let held = match reserve(store, &ids, now(), request.lease_ttl_millis).await? {
+        Reserve::Held(held) => held,
+        Reserve::Refused(refusal) => return Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(refusal)),
+    };
+    let mut attempt = Attempt::new(store, request, ids, held);
+    let ended = attempt.run(chunks, body, &mut now, &mut next_id).await;
+    attempt.finish(ended).await
+}
+
+// ───────────────────────────────── the reserve ─────────────────────────────────
+
+/// The attempt's identity, for every error it ends with.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]
+struct Ids<'a> {
+    upload_id: &'a UploadId,
+    part_number: PartNumber,
+    attempt_id: &'a AttemptId,
+}
+
+impl Ids<'_> {
+    fn stopped(&self, cause: Stop, residue: Residue) -> UploadPartError {
+        UploadPartError::Stopped(Box::new(Stopped {
+            upload_id: self.upload_id.clone(),
+            part_number: self.part_number,
+            attempt_id: self.attempt_id.clone(),
+            cause,
+            residue,
+        }))
+    }
+
+    fn in_doubt(&self, outcome: CommitUnknownResult, cause: Stop) -> UploadPartError {
+        UploadPartError::InDoubt(Box::new(InDoubt {
+            upload_id: self.upload_id.clone(),
+            part_number: self.part_number,
+            attempt_id: self.attempt_id.clone(),
+            may_still_commit: outcome.may_still_commit,
+            outcome,
+            cause,
+        }))
+    }
+}
+
+/// What a reservation came to.
+enum Reserve {
+    Held(Held),
+    Refused(Refusal),
+}
+
+/// A slot this attempt holds, and the `Open` session it holds it in.
+struct Held {
+    index: SlotIndex,
+    record: SlotRecord,
+    /// `record`, encoded: what the slot key holds.
+    slot: Bytes,
+    /// The `Open@E` session bytes the reservation was fenced on.
+    session: Bytes,
+    epoch: u64,
+}
+
+/// What one read of the session and its slot range found.
+struct ReserveRead {
+    session: Option<Bytes>,
+    /// The index holding this attempt's own slot bytes, if any.
+    own: Option<SlotIndex>,
+    /// Every index taken.
+    taken: BTreeSet<u32>,
+}
+
+async fn read_reserve(
+    store: &impl MetadataStore,
+    session_key: &[u8],
+    range: &[u8],
+    own: &Bytes,
+) -> Result<ReserveRead, Stop> {
+    let session = store.get(session_key).await.map_err(Stop::Store)?;
+    let mut read = ReserveRead {
+        session,
+        own: None,
+        taken: BTreeSet::new(),
+    };
+    for (key, value) in store.scan(range).await.map_err(Stop::Store)? {
+        let (_, index) = parse_slot_key(&key).map_err(Stop::Record)?;
+        if value == *own {
+            read.own = Some(index);
+        }
+        read.taken.insert(index.get());
+    }
+    Ok(read)
+}
+
+async fn reserve(
+    store: &impl MetadataStore,
+    ids: &Ids<'_>,
+    now_millis: u64,
+    ttl: NonZeroU64,
+) -> Result<Reserve, UploadPartError> {
+    let lease = now_millis
+        .checked_add(ttl.get())
+        .ok_or_else(|| ids.stopped(Stop::ClockOverflow, Residue::Released))?;
+    let record = SlotRecord::new(ids.part_number, ids.attempt_id.clone(), now_millis, lease)
+        .map_err(|torn| ids.stopped(Stop::Record(torn), Residue::Released))?;
+    let value = metadata::encode(&record);
+    let session_key = mpu_key(ids.upload_id);
+    let range = slot_range(ids.upload_id);
+    let budget = MAX_INFLIGHT_PARTS + UPLOAD_PART_ROUNDS;
+    let mut doubt = ReserveDoubt::default();
+    let mut commits = 0u32;
+    loop {
+        let read = match read_reserve(store, &session_key, &range, &value).await {
+            Ok(read) => read,
+            Err(stop) => return Err(doubt.end(ids, stop)),
+        };
+        let Some(session) = read.session else {
+            return Ok(Reserve::Refused(Refusal::NoSuchUpload));
+        };
+        let opened = match decode_session_record(&session) {
+            Ok(opened) => opened,
+            Err(torn) => return Err(doubt.end(ids, Stop::Record(torn))),
+        };
+        // A slot of this attempt left in a session that is no longer `Open` is the drain's.
+        if let UploadPartAnswer::Refused(refusal) = upload_part_answer(Some(opened.state())) {
+            return Ok(Reserve::Refused(refusal));
+        }
+        let epoch = opened.epoch();
+        if let Some(index) = read.own {
+            return Ok(Reserve::Held(Held {
+                index,
+                record,
+                slot: value,
+                session,
+                epoch,
+            }));
+        }
+        doubt.settle(&session, &read.taken);
+        let index = match doubt.pinned() {
+            Some(index) => index,
+            None => {
+                let free = (0..MAX_INFLIGHT_PARTS).find(|index| !read.taken.contains(index));
+                let Some(free) = free else {
+                    return Ok(Reserve::Refused(Refusal::SlowDown {
+                        pressure: Backpressure::InflightParts {
+                            max_inflight_parts: MAX_INFLIGHT_PARTS,
+                        },
+                    }));
+                };
+                match SlotIndex::new(free) {
+                    Ok(index) => index,
+                    Err(torn) => return Err(doubt.end(ids, Stop::Record(torn))),
+                }
+            }
+        };
+        if commits == budget {
+            return Err(doubt.end(ids, Stop::RoundsSpent { rounds: commits }));
+        }
+        commits += 1;
+        let key = slot_key(ids.upload_id, index);
+        let batch = WriteBatch::new()
+            .require(session_key.clone(), session.clone())
+            .require_absent(key.clone())
+            .put(key, value.clone());
+        match store.commit(batch).await {
+            Ok(CommitOutcome::Committed) => {
+                return Ok(Reserve::Held(Held {
+                    index,
+                    record,
+                    slot: value,
+                    session,
+                    epoch,
+                }))
+            }
+            // The index was taken, or the session moved: the next read says which.
+            Ok(CommitOutcome::Conflict) => {}
+            Err(fault) => match fault.downcast_ref::<CommitUnknownResult>() {
+                Some(unknown) => doubt.observe(unknown, index, &session),
+                // A definite failure of this batch; an earlier batch's doubt still stands.
+                None => return Err(doubt.end(ids, Stop::Store(fault))),
+            },
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/// What the reserve knows about its own commits whose outcome the store could not report.
+#[derive(Default)]
+struct ReserveDoubt {
+    /// **Held**: the first outcome that said `may_still_commit`, with the index that send claims
+    /// and the session bytes it requires. The reserve keeps sending to that index while it can
+    /// still land.
+    held: Option<(CommitUnknownResult, SlotIndex, Bytes)>,
+    /// **Unsettled**: the latest out-of-flight outcome no read has followed yet.
+    unsettled: Option<CommitUnknownResult>,
+}
+
+impl ReserveDoubt {
+    fn observe(&mut self, outcome: &CommitUnknownResult, index: SlotIndex, session: &Bytes) {
+        if !outcome.may_still_commit {
+            self.unsettled = Some(outcome.clone());
+        } else if self.held.is_none() {
+            self.held = Some((outcome.clone(), index, session.clone()));
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// A read that found neither this attempt's slot bytes: no out-of-flight send of it landed,
+    /// and a held one can no longer land once its session bytes are gone or another attempt
+    /// holds its index.
+    fn settle(&mut self, session: &Bytes, taken: &BTreeSet<u32>) {
+        self.unsettled = None;
+        if self
+            .held
+            .as_ref()
+            .is_some_and(|(_, index, required)| required != session || taken.contains(&index.get()))
+        {
+            self.held = None;
+        }
+    }
+
+    fn pinned(&self) -> Option<SlotIndex> {
+        self.held.as_ref().map(|(_, index, _)| *index)
+    }
+
+    fn end(self, ids: &Ids<'_>, cause: Stop) -> UploadPartError {
+        match self.held.map(|(outcome, _, _)| outcome).or(self.unsettled) {
+            Some(outcome) => ids.in_doubt(outcome, cause),
+            None => ids.stopped(cause, Residue::Released),
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+// ───────────────────────────────── the attempt ─────────────────────────────────
+
+/// One chunk whose intent landed: what the commit and the compensation name.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
+struct Staged {
+    /// The chunk as a `part:` record or a `retire:bytes:` obligation names it.
+    chunk: ChunkRef,
+    /// Its owned entry's key.
+    key: Vec<u8>,
+    /// Its planned placement, as its owned entry records it.
+    placement: StagedPlacement,
+    /// `t_auth + W_write` of the intent that landed: the deadline every fragment of it carries.
+    deadline_millis: u64,
+}
+
+/// What a batch of this attempt does if it lands, and so how a read recognises it.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
+enum Effect {
+    /// An intent: puts `value` at `staged.key` and rewrites the slot to `slot`.
+    Intent {
+        record: SlotRecord,
+        slot: Bytes,
+        staged: Staged,
+        value: Bytes,
+    },
+    /// A renewal: rewrites the slot to `slot`, and every owned lease with it.
+    Renewal { record: SlotRecord, slot: Bytes },
+    /// The commit: puts exactly `part`, and deletes the slot.
+    Commit { part: Bytes, digest: Digest },
+    /// A compensation: puts the obligation (when chunks are staged), and deletes the slot.
+    Compensation {
+        obligation: Option<(Vec<u8>, Bytes)>,
+    },
+}
+
+/// A batch of this attempt whose outcome the store could not report, and that no read has yet
+/// found landed. Every pending batch requires the slot bytes the attempt holds now.
+struct Pending {
+    effect: Effect,
+    outcome: CommitUnknownResult,
+}
+
+/// What this attempt knows about its own batches whose outcome the store could not report.
+#[derive(Default)]
+struct Doubt {
+    pending: Vec<Pending>,
+    /// **Unsettled**: the latest out-of-flight outcome no successful read has followed yet.
+    unsettled: Option<CommitUnknownResult>,
+}
+
+impl Doubt {
+    fn observe(&mut self, outcome: &CommitUnknownResult, effect: Effect) {
+        if !outcome.may_still_commit {
+            self.unsettled = Some(outcome.clone());
+        }
+        self.pending.push(Pending {
+            effect,
+            outcome: outcome.clone(),
+        });
+    }
+
+    /// A successful read that found none of the pending batches landed: the out-of-flight ones
+    /// never will, and only the held ones stay pending.
+    fn settle(&mut self) {
+        self.unsettled = None;
+        self.pending
+            .retain(|pending| pending.outcome.may_still_commit);
+    }
+
+    /// Nothing of this attempt is in doubt any more: a batch landed and moved the slot every
+    /// pending batch requires, or the session those batches require is gone for good.
+    fn clear(&mut self) {
+        self.pending.clear();
+        self.unsettled = None;
+    }
+
+    /// A commit that requires a part value now gone can never land.
+    fn drop_commits(&mut self) {
+        self.pending
+            .retain(|pending| !matches!(pending.effect, Effect::Commit { .. }));
+    }
+
+    fn holds_commit(&self) -> bool {
+        self.pending.iter().any(|pending| {
+            pending.outcome.may_still_commit && matches!(pending.effect, Effect::Commit { .. })
+        })
+    }
+
+    /// The outcome that keeps the attempt in doubt: the first held one, else the unsettled one.
+    fn standing(&self) -> Option<&CommitUnknownResult> {
+        self.pending
+            .iter()
+            .map(|pending| &pending.outcome)
+            .find(|outcome| outcome.may_still_commit)
+            .or(self.unsettled.as_ref())
+    }
+}
+
+/// What one read after a batch that did not land found.
+struct Look {
+    session: Option<Bytes>,
+    slot: Option<Bytes>,
+    part: Option<Bytes>,
+    /// The keys only this attempt's batches write (owned entries, obligations), as read.
+    witnesses: BTreeMap<Vec<u8>, Option<Bytes>>,
+}
+
+impl Look {
+    fn witness(&self, key: &[u8]) -> Option<&Bytes> {
+        self.witnesses.get(key).and_then(Option::as_ref)
+    }
+
+    /// Whether this read finds `effect`'s batch landed, by what only that batch writes.
+    fn shows(&self, effect: &Effect) -> bool {
+        match effect {
+            Effect::Intent { staged, value, .. } => self.witness(&staged.key) == Some(value),
+            Effect::Renewal { slot, .. } => self.slot.as_ref() == Some(slot),
+            Effect::Commit { part, .. } => self.part.as_ref() == Some(part),
+            Effect::Compensation {
+                obligation: Some((key, payload)),
+            } => self.witness(key) == Some(payload),
+            Effect::Compensation { obligation: None } => false,
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/// What a send came to.
+enum Sent {
+    /// A batch of this attempt landed: this one, or one sent earlier whose outcome was unknown.
+    Landed(Effect),
+    /// No batch of this attempt landed.
+    Lost(Judged),
+}
+
+/// Why no batch of this attempt landed, judged from a read.
+enum Judged {
+    /// The session is absent or no longer `Open`: the attempt's residue is the drain's.
+    Fenced,
+    /// The session is `Open` at a later epoch; these are its bytes.
+    Reopened(Bytes),
+    /// Nothing the attempt's own records show moved; the step judges the rest from the read.
+    Unmoved(Look),
+}
+
+/// How an attempt ends without an error.
+enum End {
+    /// The answer; nothing more is sent.
+    Answer(UploadPartOutcome),
+    /// Compensate what is staged, then answer this refusal.
+    Refuse(Refusal),
+}
+
+/// Why a step stopped the attempt.
+enum Halt {
+    /// Compensate what is staged, then end with this cause.
+    Compensate(Stop),
+    /// End with this cause and send nothing more: a commit of this attempt may still land, and a
+    /// compensation now would race the part it may have committed.
+    Keep(Stop),
+}
+
+impl From<Stop> for Halt {
+    fn from(stop: Stop) -> Self {
+        Self::Compensate(stop)
+    }
+}
+
+/// What a compensation came to.
+enum Compensated {
+    /// It landed: the slot is released and the obligation owes the staged chunks.
+    Done,
+    /// A commit of this attempt landed first; this is the answer.
+    Committed(UploadPartOutcome),
+    /// The session left `Open`; the residue is the drain's.
+    Fenced,
+}
+
+fn no_such_upload() -> End {
+    End::Answer(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(Refusal::NoSuchUpload))
+}
+
+struct Attempt<'a, M> {
+    store: &'a M,
+    ids: Ids<'a>,
+    scheme: EcScheme,
+    chunk_size: usize,
+    topology: &'a Topology,
+    ttl: u64,
+    window: u64,
+    session_key: Vec<u8>,
+    slot_key: Vec<u8>,
+    part_key: Vec<u8>,
+    /// The `Open@E` session bytes every batch requires.
+    session: Bytes,
+    epoch: u64,
+    /// The slot as the attempt last saw it land; every batch requires exactly `slot`.
+    record: SlotRecord,
+    slot: Bytes,
+    /// The chunks whose intent landed, in part order.
+    staged: Vec<Staged>,
+    /// The instant at or after which the leases are renewed before the next chunk.
+    renew_at: u64,
+    doubt: Doubt,
+}
+
+impl<'a, M: MetadataStore> Attempt<'a, M> {
+    fn new(store: &'a M, request: &UploadPartRequest<'a>, ids: Ids<'a>, held: Held) -> Self {
+        let ttl = request.lease_ttl_millis.get();
+        Self {
+            store,
+            ids,
+            scheme: request.scheme,
+            chunk_size: request.chunk_size.max(1),
+            topology: request.topology,
+            ttl,
+            window: request.write_window_millis.get(),
+            session_key: mpu_key(ids.upload_id),
+            slot_key: slot_key(ids.upload_id, held.index),
+            part_key: part_key(ids.upload_id, ids.part_number),
+            session: held.session,
+            epoch: held.epoch,
+            renew_at: held.record.reserved_at_millis().saturating_add(ttl / 2),
+            record: held.record,
+            slot: held.slot,
+            staged: Vec::new(),
+            doubt: Doubt::default(),
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// Stage the body chunk by chunk, then commit.
+    async fn run<B>(
+        &mut self,
+        chunks: &impl PlacementChunkStore,
+        mut body: B,
+        now: &mut impl FnMut() -> u64,
+        next_id: &mut impl FnMut() -> ChunkId,
+    ) -> Result<End, Halt>
+    where
+        B: Stream<Item = wyrd_traits::Result<Bytes>> + Unpin,
+    {
+        let mut digest = DigestBuilder::new();
+        let mut buf: Vec<u8> = Vec::with_capacity(self.chunk_size);
+        while let Some(item) = body.next().await {
+            let bytes = item.map_err(Stop::Body)?;
+            digest.update(&bytes);
+            let mut rest = &bytes[..];
+            while !rest.is_empty() {
+                let take = (self.chunk_size - buf.len()).min(rest.len());
+                buf.extend_from_slice(&rest[..take]);
+                rest = &rest[take..];
+                if buf.len() == self.chunk_size {
+                    if let Some(end) = self.stage_chunk(chunks, &buf, now, next_id).await? {
+                        return Ok(end);
+                    }
+                    buf.clear();
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        if !buf.is_empty() {
+            if let Some(end) = self.stage_chunk(chunks, &buf, now, next_id).await? {
+                return Ok(end);
+            }
+        }
+        self.commit(digest.finish(), now).await
+    }
+
+    /// End the attempt: compensate when the step asked for it, then answer or report.
+    async fn finish(
+        &mut self,
+        ended: Result<End, Halt>,
+    ) -> Result<UploadPartOutcome, UploadPartError> {
+        match ended {
+            Ok(End::Answer(outcome)) => Ok(outcome),
+            Ok(End::Refuse(refusal)) => match self.compensate().await {
+                Ok(Compensated::Done) => Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(refusal)),
+                Ok(Compensated::Committed(outcome)) => Ok(outcome),
+                Ok(Compensated::Fenced) => Ok(UploadPartOutcome::Refused(Refusal::NoSuchUpload)),
+                Err(stop) => Err(self.end(stop, Residue::Left)),
+            },
+            Err(Halt::Keep(stop)) => Err(self.end(stop, Residue::Left)),
+            Err(Halt::Compensate(stop)) => match self.compensate().await {
+                Ok(Compensated::Done) => Err(self.end(stop, Residue::Released)),
+                Ok(Compensated::Committed(outcome)) => Ok(outcome),
+                // The original cause is the one to report; whatever stopped the compensation
+                // too, the residue is left (and a doubt it raised is kept).
+                Ok(Compensated::Fenced) | Err(_) => Err(self.end(stop, Residue::Left)),
+            },
+        }
+    }
+
+    fn end(&self, cause: Stop, residue: Residue) -> UploadPartError {
+        match self.doubt.standing() {
+            Some(outcome) => self.ids.in_doubt(outcome.clone(), cause),
+            None => self.ids.stopped(cause, residue),
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// The lease the next intent or renewal stamps at `t`: a TTL past `t`, and strictly later
+    /// than the slot's current lease, so every batch changes the slot bytes it requires (the
+    /// module's "at most one landing").
+    fn next_lease(&self, t: u64) -> Result<u64, Stop> {
+        let fresh = t.checked_add(self.ttl).ok_or(Stop::ClockOverflow)?;
+        let later = self
+            .record
+            .lease_expiry_millis()
+            .checked_add(1)
+            .ok_or(Stop::ClockOverflow)?;
+        Ok(fresh.max(later))
+    }
+
+    /// The owned entry's stored value at `lease` (`0016:353`).
+    fn owned_value(&self, lease: u64, placement: &StagedPlacement) -> Bytes {
+        metadata::encode(
+            &OwnedEntry::new(self.ids.upload_id.clone(), lease, placement.clone()).to_pending(),
+        )
+    }
+
+    /// The servers with a drain record now. A key under the prefix that does not parse names no
+    /// server: the fence requires each planned server's own key ([`metadata::desired_dserver_key`]),
+    /// so leaving such a key out of the exclusion cannot place a fragment on a server whose drain
+    /// record exists.
+    async fn draining(&self) -> Result<BTreeSet<DServerId>, Stop> {
+        let records = self
+            .store
+            .scan(DESIRED_DSERVER_PREFIX)
+            .await
+            .map_err(Stop::Store)?;
+        Ok(records
+            .iter()
+            .filter_map(|(key, _)| metadata::parse_desired_dserver_key(key))
+            .collect())
+    }
+
+    fn reopen(&mut self, session: Bytes) -> Result<(), Stop> {
+        let record = decode_session_record(&session).map_err(Stop::Record)?;
+        self.epoch = record.epoch();
+        self.session = session;
+        Ok(())
+    }
+
+    fn land_rewrite(&mut self, record: SlotRecord, slot: Bytes) {
+        self.record = record;
+        self.slot = slot;
+    }
+
+    /// Send `batch`, and when it is not plainly `Committed`, read what the store holds and judge
+    /// (`0016:1597-1651`). `extra` names the keys only this batch writes that the judgement needs
+    /// besides those of the batches already pending.
+    async fn send(
+        &mut self,
+        batch: WriteBatch,
+        effect: Effect,
+        extra: &[&[u8]],
+    ) -> Result<Sent, Stop> {
+        match self.store.commit(batch).await {
+            Ok(CommitOutcome::Committed) => {
+                // It rewrote or deleted the slot every pending batch requires: none of them can
+                // land any more.
+                self.doubt.clear();
+                Ok(Sent::Landed(effect))
+            }
+            Ok(CommitOutcome::Conflict) => self.judge(extra).await,
+            Err(fault) => match fault.downcast_ref::<CommitUnknownResult>() {
+                Some(unknown) => {
+                    self.doubt.observe(unknown, effect);
+                    self.judge(extra).await
+                }
+                // A definite failure of this batch; an earlier batch's doubt still stands.
+                None => Err(Stop::Store(fault)),
+            },
+        }
+    }
+
+    async fn look(&self, extra: &[&[u8]]) -> Result<Look, Stop> {
+        let get = |key: Vec<u8>| async move {
+            let value = self.store.get(&key).await.map_err(Stop::Store)?;
+            Ok::<_, Stop>((key, value))
+        };
+        let (_, session) = get(self.session_key.clone()).await?;
+        let (_, slot) = get(self.slot_key.clone()).await?;
+        let (_, part) = get(self.part_key.clone()).await?;
+        let mut keys: BTreeSet<Vec<u8>> = extra.iter().map(|key| key.to_vec()).collect();
+        for pending in &self.doubt.pending {
+            match &pending.effect {
+                Effect::Intent { staged, .. } => {
+                    keys.insert(staged.key.clone());
+                }
+                Effect::Compensation {
+                    obligation: Some((key, _)),
+                } => {
+                    keys.insert(key.clone());
+                }
+                Effect::Renewal { .. }
+                | Effect::Commit { .. }
+                | Effect::Compensation { obligation: None } => {}
+            }
+        }
+        let mut witnesses = BTreeMap::new();
+        for key in keys {
+            let (key, value) = get(key).await?;
+            witnesses.insert(key, value);
+        }
+        Ok(Look {
+            session,
+            slot,
+            part,
+            witnesses,
+        })
+    }
+
+    /// Read, then judge: first whether a pending batch of this attempt landed, by what only it
+    /// writes; then the session; then the slot.
+    async fn judge(&mut self, extra: &[&[u8]]) -> Result<Sent, Stop> {
+        // A failed read settles nothing: the doubt stands.
+        let look = self.look(extra).await?;
+        let found = self
+            .doubt
+            .pending
+            .iter()
+            .position(|pending| look.shows(&pending.effect));
+        if let Some(found) = found {
+            let landed = self.doubt.pending.swap_remove(found).effect;
+            self.doubt.clear();
+            return Ok(Sent::Landed(landed));
+        }
+        self.doubt.settle();
+        if look.session.as_ref() != Some(&self.session) {
+            // Every batch of this attempt requires these session bytes, and an epoch that only
+            // rises never brings them back: nothing pending can land.
+            self.doubt.clear();
+            let Some(session) = look.session else {
+                return Ok(Sent::Lost(Judged::Fenced));
+            };
+            let record = decode_session_record(&session).map_err(Stop::Record)?;
+            return Ok(Sent::Lost(match record.state() {
+                SessionState::Open {} => Judged::Reopened(session),
+                SessionState::Completing { .. }
+                | SessionState::Aborting {}
+                | SessionState::Completed { .. } => Judged::Fenced,
+            }));
+        }
+        if look.slot.as_ref() != Some(&self.slot) {
+            // While the session is `Open@E` only this attempt writes its slot. Nothing pending
+            // shows by its own bytes, so a release whose evidence has since moved on is the one
+            // explanation left: a commit of this attempt that landed and was then replaced by a
+            // rival's re-upload, or a compensation that owed no chunks.
+            let release = self.doubt.pending.iter().position(|pending| {
+                matches!(
+                    pending.effect,
+                    Effect::Commit { .. } | Effect::Compensation { obligation: None }
+                )
+            });
+            let landed = release.map(|found| self.doubt.pending.swap_remove(found).effect);
+            // The slot every pending batch requires is gone either way.
+            self.doubt.clear();
+            return match landed {
+                Some(effect) => Ok(Sent::Landed(effect)),
+                None => Err(Stop::SlotLost),
+            };
+        }
+        Ok(Sent::Lost(Judged::Unmoved(look)))
+    }
+
+    // ─────────────────────────────── the steps ───────────────────────────────
+
+    /// Stage one chunk: renew if due, plan, commit the intent, then write the fragments.
+    /// `Ok(None)` goes on to the next chunk.
+    async fn stage_chunk(
+        &mut self,
+        chunks: &impl PlacementChunkStore,
+        piece: &[u8],
+        now: &mut impl FnMut() -> u64,
+        next_id: &mut impl FnMut() -> ChunkId,
+    ) -> Result<Option<End>, Halt> {
+        // The per-part ceiling, before the chunk past it is staged (`0016:1502`): a `part:`
+        // record is one value.
+        if self.staged.len() >= MAX_PART_CHUNKS as usize {
+            return Ok(Some(End::Refuse(Refusal::EntityTooLarge {
+                chunks: self.staged.len() as u64 + 1,
+                limit: u64::from(MAX_PART_CHUNKS),
+            })));
+        }
+        let t = now();
+        if t >= self.renew_at {
+            if let Some(end) = self.renew(t).await? {
+                return Ok(Some(end));
+            }
+        }
+        let id = next_id();
+        let fragments =
+            encode_chunk(self.scheme, id, piece).map_err(|fault| Stop::Encode(fault.into()))?;
+        let count = u16::try_from(fragments.len()).map_err(|fault| Stop::Encode(fault.into()))?;
+        let key = sidx_key(self.ids.upload_id, self.ids.part_number, id);
+        let mut rounds = 0u32;
+        let landed = 'plan: loop {
+            let draining = self.draining().await?;
+            let placement = select_distinct_domains(&self.topology.excluding(&draining), count)
+                .map_err(Stop::Placement)?;
+            // `t_auth`: read once, before the intent is sent, so the deadline can only be early.
+            let t_auth = now();
+            let deadline_millis = t_auth.checked_add(self.window).ok_or(Stop::ClockOverflow)?;
+            let lease = self.next_lease(t_auth)?;
+            let record = self.record.renewed(lease).map_err(Stop::Record)?;
+            let slot = metadata::encode(&record);
+            let planned =
+                StagedPlacement::new(self.scheme, placement.clone()).map_err(Stop::Record)?;
+            let value = self.owned_value(lease, &planned);
+            let staged = Staged {
+                chunk: ChunkRef {
+                    id,
+                    scheme: self.scheme,
+                    len: piece.len() as u64,
+                    placement,
+                },
+                key: key.clone(),
+                placement: planned,
+                deadline_millis,
+            };
+            let batch = self.intent_batch(&staged, &value, &slot);
+            loop {
+                if rounds == UPLOAD_PART_ROUNDS {
+                    return Err(Stop::RoundsSpent { rounds }.into());
+                }
+                rounds += 1;
+                let effect = Effect::Intent {
+                    record: record.clone(),
+                    slot: slot.clone(),
+                    staged: staged.clone(),
+                    value: value.clone(),
+                };
+                match self.send(batch.clone(), effect, &[&key]).await? {
+                    // This intent, or one of its earlier plans whose outcome was unknown.
+                    Sent::Landed(Effect::Intent {
+                        record,
+                        slot,
+                        staged,
+                        ..
+                    }) => {
+                        self.land_rewrite(record, slot);
+                        self.staged.push(staged.clone());
+                        break 'plan staged;
+                    }
+                    Sent::Landed(Effect::Renewal { record, slot }) => {
+                        // A renewal of this attempt landed late: build on the slot it wrote.
+                        self.land_rewrite(record, slot);
+                        continue 'plan;
+                    }
+                    // No commit or compensation is sent before the chunks are staged.
+                    Sent::Landed(Effect::Commit { .. } | Effect::Compensation { .. }) => {
+                        return Err(Stop::SlotLost.into());
+                    }
+                    Sent::Lost(Judged::Fenced) => return Ok(Some(no_such_upload())),
+                    Sent::Lost(Judged::Reopened(session)) => {
+                        self.reopen(session)?;
+                        return Ok(Some(End::Refuse(Refusal::OperationAborted)));
+                    }
+                    Sent::Lost(Judged::Unmoved(look)) => {
+                        if look.witness(&key).is_some() {
+                            return Err(Stop::ChunkIdTaken { chunk: id }.into());
+                        }
+                        // The drain fence: a server of this plan has a drain record now. Plan
+                        // again without it; never refuse the part for it.
+                        let draining = self.draining().await?;
+                        if staged
+                            .chunk
+                            .placement
+                            .iter()
+                            .any(|server| draining.contains(server))
+                        {
+                            continue 'plan;
+                        }
+                        // Nothing moved: an unexplained conflict, or this batch still in doubt.
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+        };
+        // Only now the bytes: each fragment to the server its owned entry names, every one with
+        // the landed intent's deadline, however late it goes out.
+        let puts =
+            fragments
+                .iter()
+                .zip(&landed.chunk.placement)
+                .map(|((index, fragment), dserver)| {
+                    chunks.put_fragment_at(
+                        *dserver,
+                        FragmentId {
+                            chunk: id,
+                            index: *index,
+                        },
+                        fragment.clone(),
+                        Some(landed.deadline_millis),
+                    )
+                });
+        futures_util::future::try_join_all(puts)
+            .await
+            .map_err(Stop::Fragments)?;
+        Ok(None)
+    }
+
+    /// The intent batch (`0016:659`).
+    fn intent_batch(&self, staged: &Staged, value: &Bytes, slot: &Bytes) -> WriteBatch {
+        let mut batch = WriteBatch::new()
+            .require(self.session_key.clone(), self.session.clone())
+            .require(self.slot_key.clone(), self.slot.clone());
+        let servers: BTreeSet<DServerId> = staged.chunk.placement.iter().copied().collect();
+        for server in servers {
+            batch = batch.require_absent(metadata::desired_dserver_key(server));
+        }
+        batch
+            .require_absent(staged.key.clone())
+            .put(staged.key.clone(), value.clone())
+            .put(self.slot_key.clone(), slot.clone())
+    }
+
+    /// Renew every lease this attempt holds at `t`: one batch puts every owned entry with the new
+    /// lease and rewrites the slot with it (`0016:349`, `:659`). A renewal that finds the session
+    /// gone from `Open` stops the attempt and recreates nothing. `Ok(None)` goes on.
+    ///
+    /// The owned entries carry no precondition of their own: while the session is `Open@E`
+    /// nothing but this attempt deletes one, and its commit and compensation delete the slot in
+    /// the same batch, so `require(mpu == Open@E)` and `require(slot == prior)` already exclude
+    /// every deleter — the drain only runs after a fence.
+    async fn renew(&mut self, t: u64) -> Result<Option<End>, Halt> {
+        let mut rounds = 0u32;
+        'build: loop {
+            let lease = self.next_lease(t)?;
+            let record = self.record.renewed(lease).map_err(Stop::Record)?;
+            let slot = metadata::encode(&record);
+            let mut batch = WriteBatch::new()
+                .require(self.session_key.clone(), self.session.clone())
+                .require(self.slot_key.clone(), self.slot.clone());
+            for staged in &self.staged {
+                batch = batch.put(
+                    staged.key.clone(),
+                    self.owned_value(lease, &staged.placement),
+                );
+            }
+            let batch = batch.put(self.slot_key.clone(), slot.clone());
+            loop {
+                if rounds == UPLOAD_PART_ROUNDS {
+                    return Err(Stop::RoundsSpent { rounds }.into());
+                }
+                rounds += 1;
+                let effect = Effect::Renewal {
+                    record: record.clone(),
+                    slot: slot.clone(),
+                };
+                match self.send(batch.clone(), effect, &[]).await? {
+                    Sent::Landed(Effect::Renewal { record, slot }) => {
+                        self.land_rewrite(record, slot);
+                        self.renew_at = t.saturating_add(self.ttl / 2);
+                        return Ok(None);
+                    }
+                    // No intent is in flight between chunks; one that landed late moved the
+                    // slot, so build on it.
+                    Sent::Landed(Effect::Intent {
+                        record,
+                        slot,
+                        staged,
+                        ..
+                    }) => {
+                        self.land_rewrite(record, slot);
+                        self.staged.push(staged);
+                        continue 'build;
+                    }
+                    Sent::Landed(Effect::Commit { .. } | Effect::Compensation { .. }) => {
+                        return Err(Stop::SlotLost.into());
+                    }
+                    Sent::Lost(Judged::Fenced) => return Ok(Some(no_such_upload())),
+                    Sent::Lost(Judged::Reopened(session)) => {
+                        self.reopen(session)?;
+                        return Ok(Some(End::Refuse(Refusal::OperationAborted)));
+                    }
+                    // Nothing moved: send it again.
+                    Sent::Lost(Judged::Unmoved(_)) => {}
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// The chunks the session's **other** parts hold, from the bounded `psum:<id>:` range
+    /// (`0016:352`). A re-upload replaces this part number's own, so it is left out.
+    async fn staged_elsewhere(&self) -> Result<u64, Stop> {
+        let summaries = self
+            .store
+            .scan(&psum_range(self.ids.upload_id))
+            .await
+            .map_err(Stop::Store)?;
+        let mut total = 0u64;
+        for (key, value) in summaries {
+            let (_, part_number) = parse_psum_key(&key).map_err(Stop::Record)?;
+            if part_number == self.ids.part_number {
+                continue;
+            }
+            let summary = decode_part_summary(&value).map_err(Stop::Record)?;
+            total = total.saturating_add(u64::from(summary.chunks));
+        }
+        Ok(total)
+    }
+
+    /// Quiesce, check the ceiling, and commit the part (`0016:660`).
+    async fn commit(&mut self, digest: Digest, now: &mut impl FnMut() -> u64) -> Result<End, Halt> {
+        // The last renewal, whose lease covers the commit (`0016:1720-1733`). The steps are
+        // sequential, so no renewal of this attempt can move the slot under the commit.
+        let t = now();
+        let fresh = t.checked_add(self.ttl).ok_or(Stop::ClockOverflow)?;
+        if fresh > self.record.lease_expiry_millis() {
+            if let Some(end) = self.renew(t).await? {
+                return Ok(end);
+            }
+        }
+        let prior = self.store.get(&self.part_key).await.map_err(Stop::Store)?;
+        // The cumulative ceiling: a read-time check, unfenced on purpose (`0016:1443-1450`).
+        let total = self
+            .staged_elsewhere()
+            .await?
+            .saturating_add(self.staged.len() as u64);
+        if total > u64::from(MAX_STAGED_CHUNKS) {
+            return Ok(End::Refuse(Refusal::EntityTooLarge {
+                chunks: total,
+                limit: u64::from(MAX_STAGED_CHUNKS),
+            }));
+        }
+        // Built once, so every send of the commit puts the same bytes: the identity a read
+        // after an unknown outcome looks for.
+        let chunks: Vec<ChunkRef> = self
+            .staged
+            .iter()
+            .map(|staged| staged.chunk.clone())
+            .collect();
+        let part = PartRecord::new(chunks, digest, t, self.epoch).map_err(Stop::Record)?;
+        let part_bytes = metadata::encode(&part);
+        let replaced = match &prior {
+            Some(bytes) => Some(decode_part_record(bytes).map_err(Stop::Record)?),
+            None => None,
+        };
+        let obligation = match replaced {
+            Some(replaced) => RetireObligation::part_chunks(
+                self.ids.upload_id,
+                self.epoch,
+                self.ids.part_number,
+                self.ids.attempt_id,
+                replaced.chunks().to_vec(),
+            )
+            .map_err(Stop::Record)?,
+            None => None,
+        };
+        let obligation_key = obligation.as_ref().map(RetireObligation::key);
+        let mut batch = WriteBatch::new().require(self.session_key.clone(), self.session.clone());
+        batch = match &prior {
+            Some(bytes) => batch.require(self.part_key.clone(), bytes.clone()),
+            None => batch.require_absent(self.part_key.clone()),
+        };
+        batch = batch.require(self.slot_key.clone(), self.slot.clone());
+        if let Some(key) = &obligation_key {
+            batch = batch.require_absent(key.clone());
+        }
+        batch = batch.put(self.part_key.clone(), part_bytes.clone()).put(
+            psum_key(self.ids.upload_id, self.ids.part_number),
+            metadata::encode(&part.summary()),
+        );
+        if let (Some(obligation), Some(key)) = (&obligation, &obligation_key) {
+            batch = batch.put(key.clone(), metadata::encode(obligation.payload()));
+        }
+        batch = batch.delete(self.slot_key.clone());
+        for staged in &self.staged {
+            batch = batch.delete(staged.key.clone());
+        }
+        let extra: Vec<&[u8]> = obligation_key.iter().map(Vec::as_slice).collect();
+        let mut rounds = 0u32;
+        loop {
+            if rounds == UPLOAD_PART_ROUNDS {
+                let stop = Stop::RoundsSpent { rounds };
+                return Err(if self.doubt.holds_commit() {
+                    Halt::Keep(stop)
+                } else {
+                    Halt::Compensate(stop)
+                });
+            }
+            rounds += 1;
+            let effect = Effect::Commit {
+                part: part_bytes.clone(),
+                digest,
+            };
+            match self.send(batch.clone(), effect, &extra).await? {
+                Sent::Landed(Effect::Commit { digest, .. }) => {
+                    return Ok(End::Answer(UploadPartOutcome::Committed {
+                        part_number: self.ids.part_number,
+                        digest,
+                    }));
+                }
+                // Nothing but this commit is in flight once the quiescing renewal has landed.
+                Sent::Landed(
+                    Effect::Intent { .. } | Effect::Renewal { .. } | Effect::Compensation { .. },
+                ) => return Err(Stop::SlotLost.into()),
+                Sent::Lost(Judged::Fenced) => return Ok(no_such_upload()),
+                Sent::Lost(Judged::Reopened(session)) => {
+                    self.reopen(session)?;
+                    return Ok(End::Refuse(Refusal::OperationAborted));
+                }
+                Sent::Lost(Judged::Unmoved(look)) => {
+                    if look.part != prior {
+                        // The losing writer (`0016:1621-1624`): a rival attempt committed this
+                        // part number. This commit requires the part bytes now gone, so it can
+                        // never land; compensate.
+                        self.doubt.drop_commits();
+                        return Ok(End::Refuse(Refusal::OperationAborted));
+                    }
+                    if let Some(key) = &obligation_key {
+                        if look.witness(key).is_some() {
+                            self.doubt.drop_commits();
+                            let key = String::from_utf8_lossy(key).into_owned();
+                            return Err(Stop::ObligationKeyTaken { key }.into());
+                        }
+                    }
+                    // Nothing moved: an unexplained conflict, or this commit still in doubt —
+                    // never compensated on that read alone. Send it again, against the same
+                    // slot bytes, so at most one of the two lands.
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// The live-session compensation (`0016:673`): one batch puts this attempt's staged chunks
+    /// as a `retire:bytes:` obligation, releases the slot and deletes every owned entry, under
+    /// `require(mpu == Open@E)` and `require(slot == prior)`. It follows the session to a later
+    /// `Open` epoch, so a rolled-back Complete never strands it (`0016:1607-1620`).
+    async fn compensate(&mut self) -> Result<Compensated, Stop> {
+        let mut rounds = 0u32;
+        'build: loop {
+            let chunks: Vec<ChunkRef> = self
+                .staged
+                .iter()
+                .map(|staged| staged.chunk.clone())
+                .collect();
+            let obligation = RetireObligation::part_chunks(
+                self.ids.upload_id,
+                self.epoch,
+                self.ids.part_number,
+                self.ids.attempt_id,
+                chunks,
+            )
+            .map_err(Stop::Record)?
+            .map(|obligation| (obligation.key(), metadata::encode(obligation.payload())));
+            let mut batch = WriteBatch::new()
+                .require(self.session_key.clone(), self.session.clone())
+                .require(self.slot_key.clone(), self.slot.clone());
+            if let Some((key, payload)) = &obligation {
+                batch = batch
+                    .require_absent(key.clone())
+                    .put(key.clone(), payload.clone());
+            }
+            batch = batch.delete(self.slot_key.clone());
+            for staged in &self.staged {
+                batch = batch.delete(staged.key.clone());
+            }
+            let extra: Vec<Vec<u8>> = obligation.iter().map(|(key, _)| key.clone()).collect();
+            let extra: Vec<&[u8]> = extra.iter().map(Vec::as_slice).collect();
+            loop {
+                if rounds == UPLOAD_PART_ROUNDS {
+                    return Err(Stop::RoundsSpent { rounds });
+                }
+                rounds += 1;
+                let effect = Effect::Compensation {
+                    obligation: obligation.clone(),
+                };
+                match self.send(batch.clone(), effect, &extra).await? {
+                    Sent::Landed(Effect::Compensation { .. }) => return Ok(Compensated::Done),
+                    Sent::Landed(Effect::Commit { digest, .. }) => {
+                        return Ok(Compensated::Committed(UploadPartOutcome::Committed {
+                            part_number: self.ids.part_number,
+                            digest,
+                        }));
+                    }
+                    // A held intent or renewal of this attempt landed first: owe what it staged
+                    // too, against the slot it wrote.
+                    Sent::Landed(Effect::Intent {
+                        record,
+                        slot,
+                        staged,
+                        ..
+                    }) => {
+                        self.land_rewrite(record, slot);
+                        self.staged.push(staged);
+                        continue 'build;
+                    }
+                    Sent::Landed(Effect::Renewal { record, slot }) => {
+                        self.land_rewrite(record, slot);
+                        continue 'build;
+                    }
+                    Sent::Lost(Judged::Fenced) => return Ok(Compensated::Fenced),
+                    Sent::Lost(Judged::Reopened(session)) => {
+                        self.reopen(session)?;
+                        continue 'build;
+                    }
+                    Sent::Lost(Judged::Unmoved(look)) => {
+                        if let Some((key, _)) = &obligation {
+                            if look.witness(key).is_some() {
+                                let key = String::from_utf8_lossy(key).into_owned();
+                                return Err(Stop::ObligationKeyTaken { key });
+                            }
+                        }
+                        // Nothing moved: send it again.
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
